+/* ── THE FACE LAW (T9-W7 CTRL-FACE) — printed, written, mono ────────────────
+   PRINTED is what the sheet came printed with: the eight group names, and only
+   those (new game · size · level · pencils · marks · candidates · checking ·
+   players). WRITTEN is what a pencil put there: every value and every verb.
+   MONO is `OptionSelector`'s OWN default and it is named here for one reason:
+   the component ships to two decks, and the deck this family does not touch
+   keeps it. A third name costs nothing and buys the shared component a face it
+   can be held to.
+   The sites read a FACE the way they read a ROLE — one token each, AT the site,
+   because a shared rule in `@layer components` loses a specificity tie to a
+   scoped component sheet and drops `font-family` in silence (measured).
